(2) It shall be the duty of every person required to be registered under subsection (1) (a) to furnish the particulars required by this Act to be entered in the register and to sign

(3) The Keeper of any specified premises shall, if so at any time by any police officer, make available for inspection any register kept in relation to those premises this section, and every register shall be open at all reasonable hours for inspection by a registration officer, or any person authorised for that purpose by a registration

(4) Any police officer, registration officer or any such authorised persons as is mentioned in subsection (3) may take an extract from any register inspected by him that subsection, and if he has reason to suspect the of any particulars entered in the register, or if any entry therein is in his opinion incomplete or misleading, he shall be entitled to demand such further information as to him to be necessary from rhe persons to whom the entry relates or from any person occupying the room to which the entry relates. ( 5) Every register kept under this section shall be Keeper of the premises to which it relates of not less than 2 years from the date of the last and may thereafter, at the discretion of the Keeper be destroyed. ( 6) Notwithstanding anything contained in this section, the registration officer may, by notice in writing under his hand, authorise the Keeper of any specified premises mentioned in the notice to keep a register in a different form (including a loose-leaf register or card index or a register is partly in the form of a bound register and partly in of a loose-leaf register or card index) from that provided by this section.
